 on  the on the trump presidency  uh it is over four years um  how how does how will saudi arabia  remember  four years of donald trump well  technically it's not over it's another  two months  but um the the kingdom of saudi arabia  has a bipartisan relationship with the  united states our relationship was  started between king abdulaziz  and franklin delano roosevelt a democrat  it continues continued through every  democratic and republican administration  and it has grown stronger and stronger  with each decade i believe that the  united states  i don't believe i know the united states  has interests around the globe saudi  arabia has interests around the globe  our interests are aligned and those  interests are not going to change  and we look forward to working with any  american administration  to further those interests the interests  might not change but the strategy  of a biden administration might be  somewhat different i mean  he he is going to have a different  relationship  with saudi arabia in the same way that  he's going to have a different  relationship  perhaps a less warm relationship with  israel for example i mean  how do you expect the next four years to  differ from the last  and are you worried about them i believe  president  elect biden was in the senate for 35  years  and he was vice president for eight  years he has tremendous experience he  knows the world  i and everybody i believe that he's  going to a point in his administration  are people that  we are likely familiar with and have  worked with  uh extensively over the years so i'm not  concerned about the  change in the american position or  american policy um  what's what happens is from one  administration to the other  the articulation might differ might  differ but the implementation really  doesn't  i wonder what your view is on on on the  fact that donald trump is insisting he  actually won the election  and the idea of a president-elect biden  is is  is not true he is still 